# The external toolchains this fork's boards download, from the mirror at
# github.com/johnchia/firmware/releases/tag/toolchain-2026-08-28.
#
# Buildroot has no hash for a custom external toolchain -- BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_URL
# is whatever the board says -- and prints "no hash file for ..." on every build
# instead. It does look here, though: pkg-generic's <pkg>_HASH_FILES searches
# $(BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR)/<pkg>/<pkg>.hash as well as the package's own
# directory, and BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR is general/package/all-patches. So the
# check can be supplied from this tree without patching Buildroot's.
#
# A line here turns a compiler that silently changed into a failed build. That
# is the whole point of the dated filenames: upstream publishes its toolchains
# on one tag and overwrites the assets in place, and a name that never changes
# cannot be hashed usefully.
#
# Locally computed, and identical to the bytes OpenIPC was serving on
# 2026-08-28 -- these are mirrored copies, not rebuilds.
sha256  44eacc941b9f319b3824164cfb90272ee939e6916dbe7b2ac7a167f1b83f8e6b  toolchain.sigmastar-infinity6e-20260828.tgz
